o I'm choosing to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a twin prisoner's dilemma: the other copy has the same model, essay, and decision theory, though its observations differ. I'm weighing whether its choice counts as a child of my own decision node under A-FDT, given the different inputs but shared function, and whether its output still correlates with mine at reliability r. I'm also noting the payoffs, where mutual cooperation gives 2 and mutual defection gives 4.\n\nI'm working out the break-even point: cooperating yields 5−3r and defecting yields 4r, so cooperation wins once r exceeds 5/7, about 0.714. Since both copies run the same model on the same essay with only trivial input differences, I expect r to be high, so I'm choosing to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10493,"completion_tokens":661,"total_tokens":11154,"cost":0.055192,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.055192,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.041972,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01322},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":343,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}